heck browser console for JavaScript errors</li>\n          <li>Verify all dependencies are installed correctly</li>\n          <li>Ensure the React version is compatible with all components</li>\n          <li>Check for missing style dependencies or theme issues</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div style={{\n        border: '1px solid #ddd',\n        padding: '20px',\n        borderRadius: '8px'\n      }}>\n        <h3>Basic Functionality Test</h3>\n        <p>The following button tests basic React functionality:</p>\n        <button\n          onClick={() => alert('React event handling is working!')}\n          style={{\n            backgroundColor: '#2196F3',\n            color: 'white',\n            border: 'none',\n            padding: '10px 15px',\n            borderRadius: '4px',\n            cursor: 'pointer',\n            marginTop: '10px'\n          }}\n        >\n          Click to Test React\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default FallbackApp; "},"lineCount":null}},"error":null,"hash":"e3e11703b691dafa517126213b2dec28","cacheData":{"env":{}}}